@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il08-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-s72-period-of-allowance`
IMPORT `nii-s335-branches`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests for s 72 (the period of the child allowance) and s 335 (the branches). Row IL-08.
-- Expected values from lines 853-856 and 3610-3620; none edited to match the code.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — sections 72 and 335`

§§ `Section 72`

GIVEN `arose`   IS A DATE
      `ended`   IS A `How the entitlement for the child ended`
      `lived`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72`
`an entitlement arising on` `arose` `, ending:` `ended` `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` `lived` `, an allowance having been paid:` `paid` MEANS
    `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72` WITH
        `the day the entitlement arose`                            IS `arose`
        `how it ended`                                             IS `ended`
        `the child lived at least seven days or left the hospital` IS `lived`
        `a child allowance was paid for the child`                 IS `paid`

-- (a): born on 10 June 2026, by the 15th: paid from 1 June. Not for May.
`born 10 June 2026` MEANS `an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `, ending:` `it has not ended` `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 6 `of` 2026 `, for` `born 10 June 2026`
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 7 `of` 2026 `, for` `born 10 June 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 5 `of` 2026 `, for` `born 10 June 2026`
-- Born on the 15th: "עד 15" includes it (fork N1). Born on the 16th: from 1 July.
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 6 `of` 2026 `, for` (`an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2026 6 15) `, ending:` `it has not ended` `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 6 `of` 2026 `, for` (`an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2026 6 16) `, ending:` `it has not ended` `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 7 `of` 2026 `, for` (`an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2026 6 16) `, ending:` `it has not ended` `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` TRUE)

-- (a), last limb: a child born 20 March 2008 turns 18 on 20 March 2026, and entitlement ceases that
-- day (row IL-06: a "child" has not reached 18). Paid to the last day of March; not for April.
`turns 18 on 20 March 2026` MEANS `an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2008 3 20) `, ending:` (`it ceased, other than by the child's death, on` (YMD 2026 3 20)) `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 3 `of` 2026 `, for` `turns 18 on 20 March 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 4 `of` 2026 `, for` `turns 18 on 20 March 2026`
-- Ceased on 1 August 2026: August paid, September not.
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 8 `of` 2026 `, for` (`an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, ending:` (`it ceased, other than by the child's death, on` (YMD 2026 8 1)) `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 9 `of` 2026 `, for` (`an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, ending:` (`it ceased, other than by the child's death, on` (YMD 2026 8 1)) `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` TRUE)

-- (c): a child for whom the allowance was paid died on 5 February 2026: paid for three months from the
-- end of February, so to the end of May; not for June.
`died 5 February 2026` MEANS `an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, ending:` (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 2 5)) `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 2 `of` 2026 `, for` `died 5 February 2026`
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 5 `of` 2026 `, for` `died 5 February 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 6 `of` 2026 `, for` `died 5 February 2026`
-- A child for whom no allowance had been paid: (c) does not reach it, and (a) ends payment with February (0.4.0: at that reading of fork N2, by name; value unchanged).
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 3 `of` 2026 `, for` (`an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, ending:` (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 2 5)) `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` FALSE) `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) runs only after an allowance was paid for the child`

-- (b): a child who lived fewer than seven days and did not leave the hospital: no allowance at all.
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 2 `of` 2026 `, for` (`an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2026 2 2) `, ending:` (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 2 5)) `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` FALSE `, an allowance having been paid:` FALSE)

-- Before May 2015: declined. The message reworded in 0.2.0 (item 08n-A2): May 2015 is this row's
-- scope, not the Law's commencement (s 402, line 4315: 1 October 1995).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 4 `of` 2015 `, for` (`an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, ending:` `it has not ended` `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` TRUE) BECAUSE "this row answers months of the child allowance from May 2015, a scope chosen to compose with row IL-06, not the commencement of the Law (s 402: 1 October 1995)"

§§ `Section 72: the period applied to every rule that gives a month (0.2.0, item 08n-GATE)`

-- Each expected value worked from line 854 before the run. The period starts with May 2015.
-- G1: arose 10 June 2026, by the 15th: (a) pays from June 2026, a month of the period: answered.
#ASSERT `s 72(a) — the first month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` `born 10 June 2026` EQUALS `s 72 — the month count of` 6 `of` 2026
-- G2: not ended: no last month.
#ASSERT `s 72(a), (c) — the last month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` `born 10 June 2026` EQUALS NOTHING
-- G3: arose 20 March 2008, after the 15th: (a) pays from April 2008, before May 2015: declined.
`born 20 March 2008, not ended` MEANS `an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2008 3 20) `, ending:` `it has not ended` `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 72(a) — the first month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` `born 20 March 2008, not ended` BECAUSE "this row answers months of the child allowance from May 2015, a scope chosen to compose with row IL-06, not the commencement of the Law (s 402: 1 October 1995)"
-- G4: the export still answers June 2026 for that child: payment began in April 2008 and has not ended.
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 6 `of` 2026 `, for` `born 20 March 2008, not ended`
-- G5, G6: the edge. Arose 20 April 2015, after the 15th: from May 2015, answered; May 2015 paid.
`arose 20 April 2015` MEANS `an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2015 4 20) `, ending:` `it has not ended` `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 72(a) — the first month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` `arose 20 April 2015` EQUALS `s 72 — the month count of` 5 `of` 2015
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 5 `of` 2015 `, for` `arose 20 April 2015`
-- G7, G8: arose 15 April 2015, by the 15th: from April 2015, before May 2015: declined; May 2015 paid.
`arose 15 April 2015` MEANS `an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2015 4 15) `, ending:` `it has not ended` `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 72(a) — the first month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` `arose 15 April 2015` BECAUSE "this row answers months of the child allowance from May 2015, a scope chosen to compose with row IL-06, not the commencement of the Law (s 402: 1 October 1995)"
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 5 `of` 2015 `, for` `arose 15 April 2015`
-- G9, G10: ceased 30 April 2015: (a) ends payment with April 2015, before May 2015: the last month is
-- declined, and May 2015 is not paid.
`ceased 30 April 2015` MEANS `an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, ending:` (`it ceased, other than by the child's death, on` (YMD 2015 4 30)) `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 72(a), (c) — the last month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` `ceased 30 April 2015` BECAUSE "this row answers months of the child allowance from May 2015, a scope chosen to compose with row IL-06, not the commencement of the Law (s 402: 1 October 1995)"
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 5 `of` 2015 `, for` `ceased 30 April 2015`
-- G11-G13: ceased 1 May 2015: the last month is May 2015, answered; May 2015 paid, June 2015 not.
`ceased 1 May 2015` MEANS `an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, ending:` (`it ceased, other than by the child's death, on` (YMD 2015 5 1)) `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72(a), (c) — the last month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` `ceased 1 May 2015` EQUALS JUST (`s 72 — the month count of` 5 `of` 2015)
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 5 `of` 2015 `, for` `ceased 1 May 2015`
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 6 `of` 2015 `, for` `ceased 1 May 2015`
-- G14-G16: died 10 February 2015, paid from January 2010 (so an allowance was paid within (a)):
-- (c), three months from the end of February 2015, to the end of May 2015: answered; May paid, June not.
`died 10 February 2015` MEANS `an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, ending:` (`the child died on` (YMD 2015 2 10)) `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72(a), (c) — the last month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` `died 10 February 2015` EQUALS JUST (`s 72 — the month count of` 5 `of` 2015)
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 5 `of` 2015 `, for` `died 10 February 2015`
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 6 `of` 2015 `, for` `died 10 February 2015`
-- G17, G18: died 10 January 2015, the same: (c) to the end of April 2015, before May 2015: declined;
-- May 2015 not paid.
`died 10 January 2015` MEANS `an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, ending:` (`the child died on` (YMD 2015 1 10)) `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 72(a), (c) — the last month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` `died 10 January 2015` BECAUSE "this row answers months of the child allowance from May 2015, a scope chosen to compose with row IL-06, not the commencement of the Law (s 402: 1 October 1995)"
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 5 `of` 2015 `, for` `died 10 January 2015`

§§ `Section 72(c): "was paid" read against (a) and (b) (0.2.0, item 08n-PAID)`

-- P1-P6: the independent tester's 72-57. Born 20 February 2026, after the 15th, so (a) pays from March
-- 2026; left the hospital; died 25 February 2026, so (a) ends payment with February. No month was
-- payable, yet an allowance is recorded as paid. February: (a) has not begun, unpaid on the text.
-- March to May 2026 (the three months (c) would add): declined. June: after the third month, unpaid on
-- either reading of (c). The first month, March 2026, is answered; the last, which turns on (c), is not.
`72-57, recorded as paid`     MEANS `an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2026 2 20) `, ending:` (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 2 25)) `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` TRUE
`72-57, recorded as not paid` MEANS `an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2026 2 20) `, ending:` (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 2 25)) `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 2 `of` 2026 `, for` `72-57, recorded as paid`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 3 `of` 2026 `, for` `72-57, recorded as paid` BECAUSE "an allowance is recorded as paid for the child, but s 72(a) and (b) make no month payable before the child died; s 72(c) does not say whether its three months follow such a payment"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 5 `of` 2026 `, for` `72-57, recorded as paid` BECAUSE "an allowance is recorded as paid for the child, but s 72(a) and (b) make no month payable before the child died; s 72(c) does not say whether its three months follow such a payment"
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 6 `of` 2026 `, for` `72-57, recorded as paid`
#ASSERT `s 72(a) — the first month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` `72-57, recorded as paid` EQUALS `s 72 — the month count of` 3 `of` 2026
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 72(a), (c) — the last month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` `72-57, recorded as paid` BECAUSE "an allowance is recorded as paid for the child, but s 72(a) and (b) make no month payable before the child died; s 72(c) does not say whether its three months follow such a payment"
-- P7, P8: the same child recorded as not paid: fork N2, (a) ends payment with February; March unpaid (0.4.0: at that reading, by name; values unchanged).
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 3 `of` 2026 `, for` `72-57, recorded as not paid` `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) runs only after an allowance was paid for the child`
#ASSERT `s 72(a), (c) — the last month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` `72-57, recorded as not paid` `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) runs only after an allowance was paid for the child` EQUALS JUST (`s 72 — the month count of` 2 `of` 2026)
-- P9-P11: (b) fails (lived three days, never left the hospital) and an allowance is recorded as paid.
-- (b) "לא תשולם קצבת ילדים אלא": no month is paid, whatever the record says; the last month,
-- which would rest on a payment (b) forbids, is declined.
`lived three days, recorded as paid` MEANS `an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2026 2 2) `, ending:` (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 2 5)) `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` FALSE `, an allowance having been paid:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 2 `of` 2026 `, for` `lived three days, recorded as paid`
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 3 `of` 2026 `, for` `lived three days, recorded as paid`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 72(a), (c) — the last month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` `lived three days, recorded as paid` BECAUSE "an allowance is recorded as paid for the child, but s 72(a) and (b) make no month payable before the child died; s 72(c) does not say whether its three months follow such a payment"
-- P12-P14: the tester's 72-56. Born 10 February 2026, by the 15th, so (a) pays February; died 20
-- February; recorded as paid, consistently: (c) to the end of May 2026. May paid, June not; last month May.
`72-56, recorded as paid` MEANS `an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2026 2 10) `, ending:` (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 2 20)) `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 5 `of` 2026 `, for` `72-56, recorded as paid`
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 6 `of` 2026 `, for` `72-56, recorded as paid`
#ASSERT `s 72(a), (c) — the last month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` `72-56, recorded as paid` EQUALS JUST (`s 72 — the month count of` 5 `of` 2026)

§§ `Section 72(c): a child who died before any allowance was paid for it (fork N2, ruled by Meng on 2026-10-08, SHRUG; version 0.4.0)`

-- Each expected value worked from lines 854-856 before the run. Default: the months the readings
-- answer differently are declined; "only after a payment" and "any child who dies while entitled"
-- asked by name.
#ASSERT `section 72(c) — the reading this row takes for a child who died before any allowance was paid for it` EQUALS `section 72(c) is declined where the two readings differ`
-- N2-1 to N2-10: born 1 January 2026, by the 15th, so (a) pays from January; left the hospital; died
-- 5 February 2026, so (a) ends payment with February; nothing recorded as paid. February: paid on
-- both readings. March to May (February + 1 to + 3): (c) on one reading, not on the other: declined.
-- June: unpaid on both. Only after a payment: last month February. Any child: last month May.
`died 5 February 2026, nothing paid` MEANS `an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, ending:` (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 2 5)) `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 2 `of` 2026 `, for` `died 5 February 2026, nothing paid`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 3 `of` 2026 `, for` `died 5 February 2026, nothing paid` BECAUSE "section 72(c) continues the allowance for three months after the death of a child for whom an allowance was paid, and does not say whether it reaches a child for whom none had yet been paid"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 5 `of` 2026 `, for` `died 5 February 2026, nothing paid` BECAUSE "section 72(c) continues the allowance for three months after the death of a child for whom an allowance was paid, and does not say whether it reaches a child for whom none had yet been paid"
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 6 `of` 2026 `, for` `died 5 February 2026, nothing paid`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 72(a), (c) — the last month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` `died 5 February 2026, nothing paid` BECAUSE "section 72(c) continues the allowance for three months after the death of a child for whom an allowance was paid, and does not say whether it reaches a child for whom none had yet been paid"
#ASSERT `s 72(a), (c) — the last month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` `died 5 February 2026, nothing paid` `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) runs only after an allowance was paid for the child` EQUALS JUST (`s 72 — the month count of` 2 `of` 2026)
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 3 `of` 2026 `, for` `died 5 February 2026, nothing paid` `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) runs for any child who dies while entitled`
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 5 `of` 2026 `, for` `died 5 February 2026, nothing paid` `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) runs for any child who dies while entitled`
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 6 `of` 2026 `, for` `died 5 February 2026, nothing paid` `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) runs for any child who dies while entitled`
#ASSERT `s 72(a), (c) — the last month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` `died 5 February 2026, nothing paid` `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) runs for any child who dies while entitled` EQUALS JUST (`s 72 — the month count of` 5 `of` 2026)
-- N2-11, N2-12: the tester's 72-57, nothing paid (born 20 February, (a) from March, died 25 February):
-- March declined at the default; paid if (c) runs for any child who dies while entitled.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 3 `of` 2026 `, for` `72-57, recorded as not paid` BECAUSE "section 72(c) continues the allowance for three months after the death of a child for whom an allowance was paid, and does not say whether it reaches a child for whom none had yet been paid"
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 3 `of` 2026 `, for` `72-57, recorded as not paid` `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) runs for any child who dies while entitled`
-- N2-13, N2-14: 72-57 recorded as paid. If (c) runs for any child who dies while entitled the record
-- is not read, and March is paid; if only after a payment, the record contradicts (a) (item 08n-PAID).
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 3 `of` 2026 `, for` `72-57, recorded as paid` `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) runs for any child who dies while entitled`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 3 `of` 2026 `, for` `72-57, recorded as paid` `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) runs only after an allowance was paid for the child` BECAUSE "an allowance is recorded as paid for the child, but s 72(a) and (b) make no month payable before the child died; s 72(c) does not say whether its three months follow such a payment"
-- N2-15: 72-56, paid within (a): (c) runs on both readings; May paid at either by name.
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 5 `of` 2026 `, for` `72-56, recorded as paid` `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) runs only after an allowance was paid for the child` AND `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 5 `of` 2026 `, for` `72-56, recorded as paid` `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) runs for any child who dies while entitled`
-- N2-16: (b) excludes the child (lived three days, never left the hospital), nothing paid: no month on
-- any reading, (b) "לא תשולם קצבת ילדים אלא".
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 3 `of` 2026 `, for` (`an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2026 2 2) `, ending:` (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 2 5)) `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` FALSE `, an allowance having been paid:` FALSE) `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) runs for any child who dies while entitled`
-- N2-17 to N2-19: died 10 March 2015, entitled since 2010, nothing paid. Only after a payment: (a) ends
-- payment with March 2015, before the period, so May 2015 is unpaid. Any child: (c) to the end of June
-- 2015, so June is paid. Default: May 2015 is within the three months: declined.
`died 10 March 2015, nothing paid` MEANS `an entitlement arising on` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, ending:` (`the child died on` (YMD 2015 3 10)) `, the child having lived seven days or left the hospital:` TRUE `, an allowance having been paid:` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 5 `of` 2015 `, for` `died 10 March 2015, nothing paid` BECAUSE "section 72(c) continues the allowance for three months after the death of a child for whom an allowance was paid, and does not say whether it reaches a child for whom none had yet been paid"
#ASSERT NOT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 5 `of` 2015 `, for` `died 10 March 2015, nothing paid` `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) runs only after an allowance was paid for the child`
#ASSERT `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` 6 `of` 2015 `, for` `died 10 March 2015, nothing paid` `, reading s 72(c) as` `section 72(c) runs for any child who dies while entitled`

§§ `Section 335`

-- Positionally, under this ruler (the order of the DECLARE in nii-il08-nouns.l4):
--  year | worker | resident | Ch 11 | housewife | widow pensioner | Ch 5 | Ch 6 | s 158(1) | controlling shareholder | Ch 8 employee | Ch 9 | long-term care
`a resident employee insured in every Chapter`          MEANS `A person in a contribution period, for section 335` OF 2026, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE
`a controlling shareholder in a closely-held company`   MEANS `A person in a contribution period, for section 335` OF 2026, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE
`a non-resident employee insured under Chapter 5 only`  MEANS `A person in a contribution period, for section 335` OF 2026, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a housewife`                                           MEANS `A person in a contribution period, for section 335` OF 2026, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE
`a widow pensioner`                                     MEANS `A person in a contribution period, for section 335` OF 2026, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE

-- An employee insured in every Chapter pays all nine (row IL-07's convention, now from the text).
#ASSERT `s 335 — the branches for which contributions are payable, for` `a resident employee insured in every Chapter` EQUALS `the branches of insurance, in the order of Schedule J`
-- (e), (f): a controlling shareholder in a closely-held company pays neither unemployment nor insolvency.
#ASSERT `s 335 — the branches for which contributions are payable, for` `a controlling shareholder in a closely-held company` EQUALS LIST `maternity`, `children`, `work injury`, `accident injury`, `disability`, `long-term care`, `senior citizens and survivors`
-- (a), (c): a non-resident employee insured for work injury only: maternity and work injury.
#ASSERT `s 335 — the branches for which contributions are payable, for` `a non-resident employee insured under Chapter 5 only` EQUALS LIST `maternity`, `work injury`
-- (b), (i): a housewife insured under Chapter 11 pays neither children nor senior citizens and
-- survivors, and (i) gives her no maternity; she pays the Chapters she is insured under.
#ASSERT `s 335 — the branches for which contributions are payable, for` `a housewife` EQUALS LIST `accident injury`, `disability`, `long-term care`
-- (i) excludes a widow pensioner; (b), which follows s 65(a)(1), excludes only a housewife.
#ASSERT `s 335 — the branches for which contributions are payable, for` `a widow pensioner` EQUALS LIST `children`, `accident injury`, `disability`, `long-term care`
-- Before 2026: declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 335 — the branches for which contributions are payable, for` (`A person in a contribution period, for section 335` OF 2025, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) BECAUSE "this row answers section 335 for contribution periods from January 2026"
